windows-launch-profile.patch -- the launch track's changes to files other
tracks own, for the coordinator to apply at integration (git apply from the
repo root). Generated with `git diff` against 731606aae plus this track's
commits; every hunk is measured in portable/docs/windows-launch-performance.md.

  spdf_win_main.cpp   (windows track)  ONE LINE: spdf_win_gpu_prewarm_start(d2d)
                      on the windowed path, right after the factories exist.
                      Without it the prewarm in spdf_win_gpu_prewarm.cpp is
                      inert and the launch is today's. Takes the file to
                      exactly 500 lines.
  spdf_win_tabs_app.h (windows track)  SPDF-LAUNCH marks around session
                      restore, spdf_open and canvas creation.
  spdf_win_window.cpp (windows track)  marks (hwnd-created, show/update-window,
                      first-paint-begin/-hwnd-target/-scene-built/-paint-end)
                      AND the two E2 hunks: build the scene before the target,
                      paint the first frame before ShowWindow. Measured -30%
                      to first page and no blank client. Takes the file to 521
                      lines: the track must extract before applying (it was
                      at 499).
  spdf_win_canvas.cpp (search track)   marks (canvas-create-begin, page0
                      measured, first-page-render-begin/-end WxH).

The marks are free when SPDF_WIN_LAUNCH_PROFILE is unset (one load, one
compare); see spdf_win_launch_profile.h.

